    "# Quiz: Common natural language processing tasks and techniques\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-2-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Tokenization</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Splits text by means of punctuation</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Punctuation can make tokenizing tricky, but the goal is to split the text into tokens, or words.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Splits text into separate tokens (words)</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Tokenization splits the text into tokens, or words. It is often the first thing NLP does.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Splits text into phrases</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Tokenization splits text into tokens, which are words, not phrases.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-2-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Embeddings</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>converts text data numerically so words can cluster</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Embeddings turn text into numbers so that words with similar meanings cluster together.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>embeds words into phrases</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Embeddings do not put words into phrases. They turn text into numbers so similar words cluster together.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>embeds sentences into paragraphs</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Embeddings do not build paragraphs. They turn text into numbers so similar words cluster together.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-2-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Parts-of-Speech Tagging</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>divides sentences by their parts of speech</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Tagging does not divide sentences. It labels each tokenized word with its part of speech, like noun or verb.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>takes tokenized words and tags them by their part of speech</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Each tokenized word is tagged with its part of speech, such as noun, verb, or adjective.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>diagrams sentences</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Tagging does not draw diagrams. It labels each tokenized word with its part of speech, like noun or verb.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
